# nr-office-quality-rendered: what the lead applies (all of it is in files this task does not own)

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-quality/src/lib.rs
Add the five module lines to the `pub mod` list, right after `pub mod presentation_acceptance;`:

    pub mod aesthetics;
    mod aesthetics_metrics;
    pub mod render_air;
    pub mod rendered;
    pub mod visual_diff;

(`aesthetics_metrics` is private: its record type and helpers are crate-internal. The module doc of lib.rs may name
the new files: `assurance-rendered`, `design-aesthetics`, `design-aesthetics-metrics`, `render-air`, `visual-diff`.)

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-quality/Cargo.toml
[dependencies]: add (the workspace already declares both):

    mixdog-raster = { workspace = true }
    base64 = { workspace = true }

[dev-dependencies] already has `base64`, `tempfile` and `mixdog-office-base` with `test-support`; the twin test and the
unit tests need nothing else (`mixdog-fsio` and `mixdog-js` are normal dependencies already).

## 3. native/core/Cargo.lock
Lead regenerates it offline. The package `mixdog-office-quality` gains the dependencies `base64` and `mixdog-raster`
(both already in the lock; no new crate enters it). `mixdog-raster` does not depend on `mixdog-office-quality`, so there
is no cycle.

## 4. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml
Nothing, unless the hakari rule wants more features unified after the two edges above: regenerate then.

## 5. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json
Run `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs --write-index` once the wave is merged: it adds the row of
the new set `office-rendered` (recorder benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-rendered.mjs, 1 file,
golden.json). The set's own MANIFEST.json is already written (native/core/fixtures/office-rendered/MANIFEST.json).

## 6. Consumers (later tasks of the track, not this one)
The tools that render and review a document call `rendered::review_rendered_office_pages(&[Value], &RenderedOptions)`
(Result: an undecodable page image is an error, as it was a rejection in Node), `rendered::{rendered_page_images,
is_small_worksheet_document}`, `aesthetics::review_rendered_office_aesthetics(&[Value], &str, &Value)`,
`render_air::{rendered_air, rendered_air_by_page}` and `visual_diff::compare_rendered_pages(proof, note, before, after,
output_pdf)`. The blocking ones run as a job on a lane (they decode and resample pictures); none is async.

## 7. Nothing else
No protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING name, no desktop fragment, no environment variable.
